(ned RACK CAL -- ONE FORK, wherever it is. Park the spindle centred about)
(10 mm above THAT holder's top, then call this with the fork number.)
(  #1 = fork number, 1 .. #3973)
()
(WHY THIS EXISTS. rack_cal walks the rack fork to fork by a FIXED pitch --)
(_rc_cy = previous - 92.0 -- and probes at the predicted centre. A holder)
(that is not on that pitch is unreachable that way: the prediction lands in)
(air and, since every move there is a probe, the cycle aborts clean without)
(ever measuring it. Operator 2026-08-16: "its situated further away, so how)
(do i probe it? its not in the linear pattern".)
()
(This calls the SAME rc_locate the walk calls, with the predicted centre)
(taken from where the operator parked instead of from the pitch. rc_locate)
(does the whole sequence -- plunge over the taper, 4-side centre, re-centre,)
(verify deeper, retract, shoulder touch -- and stores X, Y, Ztop and the)
(complete flag into 4100 + fork*4, that fork and no other.)
()
(Requires, exactly as rack_cal does: EMPTY spindle, holders energized onto)
(the toolsetter input, machine homed, probe feeds 3004-3006 set, and work)
(XYZ zeroed AT the parked pose so the Z search depths mean what they say.)

o<rack_cal_one> sub
  #<i> = #1

  o5 if [[#<i> LT 1] OR [#<i> GT #3973]]
    (abort, RACK CAL ONE: fork number must be 1 to the pocket count in 3973)
  o5 endif
  o7 if [#<_metric> EQ 0]
    (abort, RACK CAL ONE: switch to MM first)
  o7 endif

  (THE PARKED POSE IS THE DATUM, and it must be a clean one. The Z search)
  (depths below are measured FROM here, so a stale work offset would send)
  (the plunge somewhere it was never meant to go.)
  o9 if [[ABS[#<_x>] GT 0.001] OR [ABS[#<_y>] GT 0.001] OR [ABS[#<_z>] GT 0.001]]
    (abort, RACK CAL ONE: work XYZ is not zero here - zero all three at the parked pose first, centred 10 mm above this fork - NOT starting)
  o9 endif

  (predicted centre = where we are. This is the ONLY difference from the)
  (walk, and it is the whole point: no pitch, no interpolation.)
  #<_rc_cx>   = #<_x>
  #<_rc_cy>   = #<_y>
  #<_rc_safe> = #<_z>
  (find 20 mm below the parked pose - operator 2026-08-16. One fork has no)
  (previous tool top to work from, so it always uses the parked -20 rule.)
  #<_rc_pfind> = [#<_z> - 20.0]
  (VERIFY DEPTH 60, operator 2026-08-16: at 70 it was reaching the)
  (drawbar inside the spindle bore, not the taper. Same failure mode)
  (as the 75 -> 70 change on 2026-08-04, one step further out.)
  (This is also the bottom end of the fast-probe ramp, so the ramp)
  (now spans 20..60 rather than 20..70 and reaches #3005 at 60.)
  #<_rc_p60>  = [#<_z> - 60.0]
  (REACH FOLLOWS THE FIND LEVEL. 8.0 was sized for the old -50)
  (descent. The find now happens at -20, 30 mm higher, and the)
  (spindle taper is ISO-30 -- 7:24 per docs/components.md -- so its)
  (radius shrinks 0.14583 mm per mm of Z: 30 * 3.5/24 = 4.375 mm)
  (more bore-to-taper gap on every side. The 8.0 probe ran out of)
  (travel before the taper and G38.2 raised its own no-contact)
  (error, which fires before rc_touch's guard can say anything.)
  (12.4 is the geometric floor; 14.0 was still short on the iron,)
  (so the operator called 18.0 on 2026-08-16. A longer reach costs)
  (nothing when the taper is there -- contact stops the probe.)
  #<_rc_reach> = 18.0
  #<_rc_ftr>  = #3006
  #<_rc_fpr>  = #3004
  (_rc_fpr0 is the UNSCALED fast probe and _rc_ptop the Z at which it)
  (is used in full. rc_locate overwrites _rc_fpr per find level, so the)
  (original has to survive somewhere or every fork after the first)
  (would inherit the previous fork's reduced feed.)
  #<_rc_fpr0> = #3004
  #<_rc_ptop> = [#<_z> - 20.0]
  #<_rc_fla>  = #3005
  #<_rc_fck>  = #3004
  o8 if [[#<_rc_ftr> LE 0] OR [#<_rc_fpr> LE 0] OR [#<_rc_fla> LE 0]]
    (abort, RACK CAL ONE: probe feeds 3004-3006 are not set - set them on the probe screen first)
  o8 endif

  (PRINT, RACK CAL ONE: locating fork #<i> from the parked pose)
  o<rc_locate> call [#<i>]
  (PRINT, RACK CAL ONE: fork #<i> stored - no other fork was touched)

o<rack_cal_one> endsub
